# WF-RV-01 — Removed Code Review File (Official)

## Purpose

`AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` is the **official temporary archive of removed/replaced code** for architectural review.

It exists because the Cursor review UI no longer allows reliable selection/copy of deleted blocks.

It is **not** a diff, changelog, or patch. It contains **only** code that would be lost if the modified files are accepted.

**Invariant:** the file must **always** contain **exclusively** files still in review (and their removed code). It must **never** become a permanent history of already-accepted changes.

## Naming

- Primary: `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` (repo root)
- Alias (legacy): `AI_REMOVED_CODE_REVIEW.md` — prefer the primary name

## Rule 1 — One document

There is **exactly one** `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md`. It accompanies the review until conclusion.

## Rule 2 — Incremental document

The file must represent **all** changes still in review, not only the latest edit.

- Modify File A → add/update A blocks
- Modify File B → add/update B blocks
- Modify File C → add/update C blocks

Blocks for earlier files **must not** be deleted by a later generation pass.

## Rule 3 — When blocks may be removed (acceptance closes review)

Blocks for a file may be removed **only** when that file’s review is **closed by acceptance**.

### What counts as acceptance

Any clear user confirmation that one or more files are accepted / approved closes their review, including (not limited to):

- explicit **ACCETTO** / «accetto» / «accettati» after ChatGPT (or other) review;
- confirmation that those files are accepted and no longer under review;
- equivalent wording that the review for those paths is done.

Accepted files are **no longer “in review”**.

### Mandatory automatic cleanup (no user reminder)

**Immediately** after acceptance, the agent **MUST** run the WF-RV-01 cleanup for **every** accepted path — equivalent to `--accept` — and remove **all** blocks for those files from `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md`.

The user must **never** have to remember or request this cleanup manually.

Until acceptance, keeping those blocks is mandatory. Losing them early is a **workflow regression**. Leaving accepted files in the document is also a **workflow regression**.

## Rule 4 — Mandatory block format

Every removal block **must** use exactly this structure (fields in this order):

1. Separator line: `================================================================================`
2. `# FILE` then the full path on its own line
3. `## FUNZIONE / SEZIONE` then the name (or `Sezione non identificabile`)
4. `## CODICE RIMOSSO` then a fenced code block with **only** removed/replaced (old) lines
5. `## MOTIVO` then at most three lines (why removed / which behavior it replaces — never describe the new code)

### FUNZIONE / SEZIONE

- Prefer function, component, or hook name.
- Otherwise a short section description.
- If unknown: exactly `Sezione non identificabile` (never empty).

### CODICE RIMOSSO

- Only lines actually removed or replaced (old version).
- No added code, unified diff, `+`/`-` markers, or unchanged context.
- Use the correct fence language (`tsx`, `ts`, `sql`, `md`, …).

### MOTIVO

- Maximum **three** lines.
- Why it was removed, or what behavior it replaces.
- Do **not** describe the new code.

## Rule 5 — Ordering

1. By file path (stable order of appearance in the document; newly touched files append after existing files unless regenerating that file in place).
2. Within a file, blocks in the order removals appear in the file (diff order).

Never random order.

## Rule 6 — Goal

Enable a full review of deleted code **without** the Cursor diff viewer.

## Rule 7 — No information loss (while in review)

While a file is unaccepted, its removed code **must** remain in the document.

## Rule 8 — Compatibility

Consolidation only: same naming, philosophy, and operating mode. No change to product application code via this workflow rule alone.

## Rule 9 — Implementation scope

Update only WF-RV-01 workflow docs and the generator (`scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js`). Do not change application/runtime/services/DB/AI_CONTEXT/AI_CONTEXT_MASTER as part of WF-RV-01 maintenance.

## Rule 10 — Report operativo (mandatory when the archive changes)

Every time the agent modifies `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` (generation **or** cleanup), the final **Report operativo** **MUST** declare it explicitly.

The modified-files list **MUST** always include:

- `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md`

with the reason:

- `aggiornato (nuove eliminazioni)` — after merge/generation; **or**
- `pulito dopo accettazione file (workflow WF-RV-01)` — after `--accept` cleanup

**Never** omit this file from the report when it was modified.

## Agent operating procedure (mandatory)

### After any AI change set that touches files

1. Complete the code/doc edits.
2. Update `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` **incrementally**:
   - refresh blocks for files touched in this change;
   - **preserve** blocks for other files still in review;
   - use the mandatory format above.
3. Prefer: `node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js` (merge mode) from repo root.
4. Declare `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` in the Report operativo (`aggiornato (nuove eliminazioni)`).
5. Never commit `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` (gitignored). Never ask the user to accept it as project source.

### When the user accepts one or more files

1. Treat those paths’ review as **closed** (no longer in review).
2. **Immediately** run cleanup for all accepted paths, e.g.:
   - `node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js --accept=path/to/File.tsx`
   - or comma-separated / repeated: `--accept=a.tsx,b.ts`
3. Confirm the document no longer contains sections for accepted files.
4. Declare `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` in the Report operativo (`pulito dopo accettazione file (workflow WF-RV-01)`), listing which paths were cleaned.

## Generator CLI

```text
node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js
node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js --files=a.tsx,b.ts
node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js --accept=src/path/File.tsx
node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js --accept=a.tsx,b.ts
```

- Default / `--files=…`: merge-update those paths (or all dirty paths if omitted); keep other existing file sections.
- `--accept=…`: drop sections for those path(s) only (comma-separated and/or repeated `--accept=`).

## Repository policy

`AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` / `AI_REMOVED_CODE_REVIEW.md`:

- MUST NEVER be committed
- MUST NEVER be merged as source of truth
- Discard after the overall review is complete

Official long-form copy: `AI_DEV_WORKFLOW/WORKFLOWS/WF_RV_01_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md`
